\title{Latest Deep-Dive}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-19}
\meta{toc}{true}

\p{
    See my latest on [soundness notions](dhsorens-002F) — the five things \em{sound} can mean in the
    security theorem for a SNARK, the implications between them, and which of them survives
    [Fiat–Shamir](dhsorens-002G). The short version is that compilation chooses a notion rather than
    inheriting one, which is why a protocol proved sound end-to-end has not yet been proved anything
    about its deployed form. It is the first written-out section of the [zkVMs and
    SNARKs](dhsorens-002C) corpus.
}
